# Recorded keystroke data stays on the machine that recorded it.
#
# Two reasons, both firm:
#
#   * It is sensitive. Every clip is a recording of someone typing, and
#     _sessions/*.json is a literal keylog - the keysym, character and
#     timestamp of each press. Whatever was typed while recording is in
#     here, including anything typed by mistake into the wrong window.
#   * It would not help anyone else anyway. A keystroke model only holds up
#     on the exact microphone, keyboard, distance and room it was recorded
#     on, so another person's clips are worthless as training data for you -
#     and mixing them in makes a model worse, not better.
#
# So: ignore the contents, keep the folder. A fresh clone still gets an empty
# dataset/ for the annotator to write into.
#
# Collect your own with:  python train_keystroke_classifier.py

*
!.gitignore
